FINDING: Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/StoreController.php@get_details never calls
Log:: on either the 403 out_of_zone branch or the 200 success branch (confirmed by
reading the method AND by this live positive+negative control, both zero-hit) — a
pre-existing backend observability gap, NOT introduced by this diff (this ticket's
diff touches only UserApp/lib/features/cart/screens/cart_screen.dart). Because BOTH
the failing and the passing request produce zero log lines, the log instrument is
"dead" for this endpoint, not selectively silent -- the positive control does not
distinguish the two cases, so the literal log-grep method specified by AC2 is
currently inconclusive on its own.

Substance of AC2 (classification is the SAME pre-existing out_of_zone path already
used by Checkout, not a new/different backend error path) is instead demonstrated by:
  1. Single PHP route/controller method for this endpoint: routes/api/v1/api.php:350
     `Route::get('stores/details/{id}', 'StoreController@get_details')` — both
     Checkout (checkout_controller.dart:465 initCheckoutData) and Cart (this fix,
     cart_screen.dart:113) call the identical Dart StoreController.getStoreDetails
     -> storeServiceInterface.getStoreDetails -> this one endpoint. There is no
     second/parallel store-details path.
  2. Same classification helper: StoreController.php:186 checks
     `Helpers::storeZoneAllowed($store, $request)` (Helpers.php:5353) -> the same
     403 {"code":"out_of_zone"} shape captured above, unconditionally of caller.
  3. Live curl reproduction (above) matches the exact shape previously captured for
     the SAME zone-guard mechanism at docs/qa-evidence/NEARS-1113/ZONEGUARD-store12-zone1.txt.
  4. FE-side: store_controller.dart:963-980 is the ONE classification branch reached
     by both callers, emitting the paired AppLogger.warn + AppLogger.failure(status
     403, code out_of_zone, correlationId=<echoed X-Request-Id>) regardless of
     fromCart/checkout caller -- confirmed live via `flutter test` run (see
     ac1-flutter-test-log.txt) and again live from the device (see ac1 evidence).

